From f98d12fa81e73bf2d508494a49754ff7be084563 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini engine authoring <engine@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:45:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fill OptiX instances and motion transforms in parallel

After batching the motion transform upload, the remaining host cost of
the OptiX top-level build is filling one OptixInstance and, for moving
objects, decomposing the motion and writing its OptixSRTMotionTransform,
serially for every object and again for every device.

Assign instance slots and motion transform offsets in object order first,
then fill them with parallel_for; each object writes only its own instance
and motion transform. Traversable handles are converted afterwards on the
calling thread, so no OptiX call is made from worker threads. Instance
order, offsets and contents are unchanged.

Rationale: Per-object instance and motion transform preparation remained serial per device and dominated the top-level build with hundreds of thousands of moving instances.
Contract: Instance descriptions, motion transform bytes, offsets and traversable handles are identical to the serial loop; OptiX API calls stay on the calling thread.
Tests: tests/houdini_packed_velocity_smoke.py, tests/houdini_motion_smoke.py, tests/houdini_velocity_motion_smoke.py, tests/houdini_packed_deformation_smoke.py, tests/houdini_sampled_instance_attribute_smoke.py, tests/houdini_multi_gpu_animation_smoke.py
